    <article class="intro-card digcomp-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">The capability foundation</p>
      <h2>What is DigComp 3.0?</h2>
      <p>
        DigComp 3.0 is the latest edition of the European Digital Competence Framework. Developed by the European Commission, it describes the knowledge, skills and attitudes people need to use digital technologies confidently, critically and responsibly at work, in learning and when participating in society.
      </p>
      <p>
        DigComp provides a shared, technology-neutral way to:
      </p>
      <ul class="scannable-list compact-list">
        <li>understand digital capability</li>
        <li>assess strengths and development needs</li>
        <li>design learning and development</li>
        <li>support applied workplace learning</li>
        <li>track capability uplift</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        It covers five competence areas and 21 competences. DigComp 3.0 also reflects developments in artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, digital rights, wellbeing, inclusion, sustainability, and misinformation and disinformation. AI capability is integrated across the framework.
      </p>
      <h3>How DigComp fits in Queensland and Australia</h3>
      <p>
        DigComp informs the Queensland public sector Digital Capability Framework, which supports individuals, leaders and organisations to build digital skills, adapt to changing technology and improve services. The Queensland framework also draws on SFIA and the Australian Public Service Data Capability Framework.
      </p>
      <p>
        At the national level, the Australian Government recognises DigComp and SFIA as preferred guides for digital skills and training. DigComp can help employers, educators, learners and workers understand and develop digital capability across industries and occupations.
      </p>
